IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 9, Citation of Acts and instruments
-- (ss 38 to 40A). Sections 41 to 45 are repealed (endnote 4).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Whether an old and a new provision "correspond" (s 40A(4))
-- is decided by other Acts (Part 10.1 of the Corporations Act 2001 and Part 16 of the ASIC
-- Act 2001), which are not in this text: it is an INPUT.

§ `Part 9: Citation of Acts and instruments`

§§ `Section 38: reference to Acts`

DECLARE `Law-making body` IS ONE OF
    `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`
    `the Parliament of the United Kingdom`
    `the Parliament of a State`
    `the legislature of a Territory`

-- src:828 | 38 Reference to Acts
-- src:829 | (1) An Act passed by the Parliament of the Commonwealth may be referred to by the word “Act” alone.
-- src:830 | (2) An Act passed by the Parliament of the United Kingdom may be referred to by the term “Imperial Act”.
-- src:831 | (3) An Act passed by the Parliament of a State may be referred to by the term “State Act”.
-- src:832 | (4) An Act passed by the legislature of a Territory may be referred to by the term “Territory Act”.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 38 (src:828-832)
GIVEN body IS A `Law-making body`
GIVETH A STRING
`the term by which an Act of this body may be referred to` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` THEN "Act"
    WHEN `the Parliament of the United Kingdom` THEN "Imperial Act"
    WHEN `the Parliament of a State` THEN "State Act"
    WHEN `the legislature of a Territory` THEN "Territory Act"

§§ `Section 39: numbering of Acts`

-- The Acts passed in a secular year are numbered 1, 2, 3 ... in the order of assent. Two Acts
-- assented to on the same day are ordered by the order in which the Governor-General assents
-- to them, which this text does not otherwise record; the count of earlier assents is the input.
-- src:833 | 39 Numbering of Acts
-- src:834 | The Acts passed in each secular year shall be numbered in regular arithmetical series, beginning with the number 1, in the order in which the Governor-General assents thereto, or makes known the Sovereign’s assent thereto.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 39 (src:833-834)
GIVEN `the number of Acts assented to earlier in the same secular year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number given to the Act` `the number of Acts assented to earlier in the same secular year` MEANS
    `the number of Acts assented to earlier in the same secular year` PLUS 1

§§ `Section 40: citation of Acts and instruments`

DECLARE `Thing cited` IS ONE OF
    `a Commonwealth Act`
    `a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    `an Imperial Act`
    `a State Act`
    `a Territory Act`

DECLARE `Way of citing` IS ONE OF
    `its short title`
    `the secular year in which it was passed, and its number`
    `a unique identifier given in accordance with rules prescribed under the Legislation Act 2003`
    `any name the instrument gives itself`
    `the year it was made and its number, with a reference to the kind of instrument if necessary`
    `the date and, if necessary, number and page of the Gazette in which it was notified or published`
    `the date it was made, with a reference to the Act or instrument, and provision if necessary, under which it was made`
    `a reference to the State or Territory whose Parliament or legislature passed it, with a mode of reference sufficient in Acts of that Parliament or legislature`
    `another manner sufficient in an Imperial Act`
    `a reference to the part, section, subsection or other division in which the enactment is contained`

-- src:836 | Citation of Acts, legislative instruments and notifiable instruments
-- src:837 | (1A) In any Act, instrument or document:
-- src:838 | (a) an Act may be cited by:
-- src:839 | (i) the short title of the Act; or
-- src:840 | (ii) the secular year in which it was passed, and its number; or
-- src:841 | (iii) a unique identifier given to the Act in accordance with rules prescribed under the Legislation Act 2003; and
-- src:842 | (b) a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument may be cited by:
-- src:843 | (i) any name the instrument gives itself; or
-- src:844 | (ii) a unique identifier given to the instrument in accordance with rules prescribed under the Legislation Act 2003; or
-- src:845 | (iii) if the instrument was numbered under a Commonwealth law—the year it was made and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to the kind of instrument; or
-- src:846 | (iv) if the instrument was notified or published in the Gazette—the date and (if necessary) number and page of the Gazette in which it was notified or published; or
-- src:847 | (v) the date it was made, together with a reference to the Act or instrument, and (if necessary) provision, under which it was made.
-- src:848 | Citation of Imperial Acts, State Acts and Territory Acts
-- src:849 | (1) In any Act, instrument, or document:
-- src:850 | (b) any Imperial Act may be cited by its short title (if any) or in such other manner as is sufficient in an Imperial Act; and
-- src:851 | (c) any State Act may be cited by a reference to the State by the Parliament whereof the Act was passed, together with such mode of reference as is sufficient in Acts passed by such Parliament; and
-- src:852 | (d) any Territory Act may be cited by a reference to the Territory by whose legislature the Act was passed, together with such mode of reference as is sufficient in Acts passed by that legislature.
-- src:853 | (2) Any enactment may be cited by reference to the part, section, subsection, or other division of the Act, Imperial Act, State Act or Territory Act, in which the enactment is contained.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 40(1A), (1) and (2) (src:836-853)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing cited`
      way IS A `Way of citing`
      `it has a short title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument was numbered under a Commonwealth law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument was notified or published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it may be cited this way in an Act, instrument or document` thing way `it has a short title` `the instrument was numbered under a Commonwealth law` `the instrument was notified or published in the Gazette` MEANS
        way EQUALS `a reference to the part, section, subsection or other division in which the enactment is contained`
    OR (CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `a Commonwealth Act` THEN
                way EQUALS `its short title`
             OR way EQUALS `the secular year in which it was passed, and its number`
             OR way EQUALS `a unique identifier given in accordance with rules prescribed under the Legislation Act 2003`
        WHEN `a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN
                way EQUALS `any name the instrument gives itself`
             OR way EQUALS `a unique identifier given in accordance with rules prescribed under the Legislation Act 2003`
             OR (way EQUALS `the year it was made and its number, with a reference to the kind of instrument if necessary` AND `the instrument was numbered under a Commonwealth law`)
             OR (way EQUALS `the date and, if necessary, number and page of the Gazette in which it was notified or published` AND `the instrument was notified or published in the Gazette`)
             OR way EQUALS `the date it was made, with a reference to the Act or instrument, and provision if necessary, under which it was made`
        WHEN `an Imperial Act` THEN
                (way EQUALS `its short title` AND `it has a short title`)
             OR way EQUALS `another manner sufficient in an Imperial Act`
        WHEN `a State Act` THEN
             way EQUALS `a reference to the State or Territory whose Parliament or legislature passed it, with a mode of reference sufficient in Acts of that Parliament or legislature`
        WHEN `a Territory Act` THEN
             way EQUALS `a reference to the State or Territory whose Parliament or legislature passed it, with a mode of reference sufficient in Acts of that Parliament or legislature`)

§§ `Section 40A: references to the new corporations and ASIC legislation`

-- src:854 | 40A References to the new corporations and ASIC legislation
-- src:855 | (1) A reference in an Act to:
-- src:856 | (a) an Act, or regulations or another instrument, that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation; or
-- src:857 | (b) a provision, or group of provisions, of such an Act, regulations or other instrument;
-- src:858 | is taken to include a reference to:
-- src:859 | (c) the corresponding part, provision or provisions of the old corporations legislation or the old ASIC legislation; and
-- src:860 | (d) any relevant earlier law.
-- src:861 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to:
-- src:862 | (a) a reference in an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation; or
-- src:863 | (b) a reference in the Corporations (Repeals, Consequentials and Transitionals) Act 2001; or
-- src:864 | (c) a reference that identifies an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation as an Act to be amended; or
-- src:865 | (d) a reference in a provision that applies an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation, or a provision or group of provisions, of such an Act to a particular matter (whether with or without modification).
-- src:866 | (3) Subsection (1) has effect:
-- src:867 | (a) subject to an express provision to the contrary in the Act concerned; and
-- src:868 | (b) subject to regulations made for the purposes of subsection (5).
-- src:869 | (4) For the purposes of this section:
-- src:870 | (a) the question whether a part, provision or provisions of the old corporations legislation corresponds to a part, provision or provisions of the new corporations legislation is to be determined in the same way as it is determined for the purposes of Part 10.1 of the Corporations Act 2001; and
-- src:871 | (b) the question whether a part, provision or provisions of the old ASIC legislation corresponds to a part, provision or provisions of the new ASIC legislation is to be determined in the same way as it is determined for the purposes of Part 16 of the Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001.
-- src:872 | (5) The regulations may provide that subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a particular reference, or class of references, in an Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 40A(1) to (5) (src:854-872)
GIVEN `the reference is to an Act, regulations or other instrument that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation, or to a provision or group of provisions of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in the Corporations (Repeals, Consequentials and Transitionals) Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference identifies an Act of the new legislation as an Act to be amended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in a provision that applies an Act of the new legislation, or a provision of one, to a particular matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act concerned expressly provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations made for subsection (5) exclude this reference or class of references` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference is taken to include the corresponding old provision and any relevant earlier law` `the reference is to an Act, regulations or other instrument that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation, or to a provision or group of provisions of one` `the reference is in an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation` `the reference is in the Corporations (Repeals, Consequentials and Transitionals) Act 2001` `the reference identifies an Act of the new legislation as an Act to be amended` `the reference is in a provision that applies an Act of the new legislation, or a provision of one, to a particular matter` `the Act concerned expressly provides to the contrary` `regulations made for subsection (5) exclude this reference or class of references` MEANS
        `the reference is to an Act, regulations or other instrument that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation, or to a provision or group of provisions of one`
    AND (NOT `the reference is in an Act that is part of the new corporations legislation or the new ASIC legislation`)
    AND (NOT `the reference is in the Corporations (Repeals, Consequentials and Transitionals) Act 2001`)
    AND (NOT `the reference identifies an Act of the new legislation as an Act to be amended`)
    AND (NOT `the reference is in a provision that applies an Act of the new legislation, or a provision of one, to a particular matter`)
    AND (NOT `the Act concerned expressly provides to the contrary`)
    AND (NOT `regulations made for subsection (5) exclude this reference or class of references`)
